      "body": "**TLDR:** The Verifiers generation server logged one INFO line per generate call: 79-87% of the controller's log lines and ~6-9% of the controller thread's samples. `AppRunner(access_log=None)` turns it off.\n\n**Stack** (14 PRs, merge bottom-up; this PR is in **bold**)\n\n| # | PR | Independent? | Needs (stack positions) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Verifiers 0.4.0 | yes | — |\n| 2 | Verifiers: release each finished rollout's routing session | yes | — (resolves its test overlap with 1) |\n| **3** | **Verifiers generation server: no per-request access log** | **yes** | **—** |\n| 4 | Verifiers generation server: faster request path, required sampling params | yes | — (resolves its test overlap with 1-3) |\n| 5 | Rollout workers write structured logs | yes | — |\n| 6 | Drain in-flight rollouts during shutdown | yes | — |\n| 7 | Generator drains itself before a hot_swap=False weight load | yes | — |\n| 8 | Move GenerationServer to torchtitan/rl/generator | yes, in code | — (moves the file 3 and 4 edit) |\n| 9 | Every generate call goes over HTTP to its generator | no | 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8 |\n| 10 | Generator aborts a request whose caller left | no | 9 |\n| 11 | Cancel a rollout group on its worker | no | 5, 6, 9 |\n| 12 | Run Verifiers groups in rollout workers | no | 9, 11 |\n| 13 | Optional native rollout timeout | no | 12 |\n| 14 | Rollouts that fail outside the policy are recorded, not trained | no | 12, 13 |\n\n**Results**\n```text\nTerminal-Bench RL runs on GB300, controller log\naiohttp.access lines    79-87% of lines (4 runs)\n                        1.7-2.0M lines, 334-386 MB (the two longest runs)\n\npy-spy --gil, controller thread, 120 s, 10-node SWE RL run\naccess log + logging    ~6-9% of samples\n```\n\nYou may ask:\n- What about errors? Every response loses its access line, errors included. A `GenerateFn` exception still logs with `logger.exception`; other error responses reach the client, and failed rollouts log their reason.\n- Where is per-call timing? Each generate call still gets a `generate` span in the controller's structured log.\n\n**Test plan**\n```bash\npytest tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_verifiers.py -k generation_server\n```\n`test_generation_server_does_not_log_each_request` fails on main. It pins the `aiohttp.access` logger at INFO, since aiohttp skips the line above INFO and the inherited level depends on imports.\n",
